		</div>
	{/snippet}
</AdaptiveList>
</div>

- Proxy URLs take the form `scheme://user:pass@host:port`, where the scheme is `http`, `socks5`, or `socks5h`. Use `socks5h` to send DNS lookups through the proxy too.
- Special characters in the username or password need to be URL-encoded, such as `@` as `%40` and `:` as `%3A`.

<Callout type="warning">

Add your Radarr and Sonarr instances and the parser to `NO_PROXY`. Any host that isn't listed is sent to the proxy, and the proxy usually can't reach services on your local network. This matters most when `HTTP_PROXY` or `ALL_PROXY` is set, since those also cover plain `http://` addresses.

</Callout>

For example, this routes Profilarr through a proxy container named `gluetun`, while your Arrs and the parser stay direct:

<CodeBlock items={proxyExample} />

